# Files that Linux executes or that dpkg reads must stay LF whatever core.autocrlf says on the
# machine that checked them out: a postinst with CRLF line endings fails at "#!/bin/sh
".
*.sh text eol=lf
packaging/linux/deb/* text eol=lf
packaging/udev/* text eol=lf

# Applied with `git apply` inside WSL against an LF-only Rust repository, so CRLF makes every hunk
# fail to match and bench.ps1 -Build reports a patch that "does not apply". Same class as the
# postinst above: the file is consumed by Linux tooling, not by anything on Windows.
testbench/virtual-qa40x/*.patch text eol=lf

# The charting engine. Git would autodetect it, but this file has rules precisely because
# line-ending conversion has bitten before, and a corrupted wasm fails only at run time.
*.wasm binary
